ex:C045R0018 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Termination — source passage 103" ;
    ct:kind "TERMINATION" ;
    ct:subject_to ex:C045R0018Condition103 ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0103 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

ex:C045R0018Condition103 a ct:Condition ;
    ct:description "14.4 Liquidated Damages on Termination.   14.4.1 Calculation of Liquidated Damages. You acknowledge and agree that the premature termination of this Agreement will cause substantial damage to us. You agree that Liquidated Damages are not a penalty, but represent a reasonable estimate of the minimum just and fair compensation for the damages we will suffer as the result of your failure to operate the Hotel for the Term. If this Agreement terminates before the Expiration Date, you will pay us Liquidated Damages as follows:   14.4.1.1 If termination occurs before you begin the Hotel Work and before the Opening Date, and you or any Guarantor (or your or any Guarantor's Affiliates) directly or indirectly, enter into a franchise, license, management, lease and/or other similar agreement for or begin construction or commence operation of a hotel, motel, inn, or similar facility at the Hotel Site under a Competitor Brand within one (1) year after termination, then you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount equal to $3,600 multiplied by the number of approved Guest Rooms at the Hotel.   14.4.1.2 If termination occurs after you begin the Hotel Work but before the Opening Date, you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount equal to $3,600 multiplied by the number of approved Guest Rooms at the Hotel, unless your failure to complete the Hotel Work was the result of Force Majeure.   " ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0103 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

ex:C045R0019 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Conditional Referenced Term — source passage 103" ;
    ct:kind "CONDITIONAL_REFERENCED_TERM" ;
    ct:subject_to ex:C045R0019Condition103 ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0103 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

ex:C045R0019Condition103 a ct:Condition ;
    ct:description "14.4 Liquidated Damages on Termination.   14.4.1 Calculation of Liquidated Damages. You acknowledge and agree that the premature termination of this Agreement will cause substantial damage to us. You agree that Liquidated Damages are not a penalty, but represent a reasonable estimate of the minimum just and fair compensation for the damages we will suffer as the result of your failure to operate the Hotel for the Term. If this Agreement terminates before the Expiration Date, you will pay us Liquidated Damages as follows:   14.4.1.1 If termination occurs before you begin the Hotel Work and before the Opening Date, and you or any Guarantor (or your or any Guarantor's Affiliates) directly or indirectly, enter into a franchise, license, management, lease and/or other similar agreement for or begin construction or commence operation of a hotel, motel, inn, or similar facility at the Hotel Site under a Competitor Brand within one (1) year after termination, then you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount equal to $3,600 multiplied by the number of approved Guest Rooms at the Hotel.   14.4.1.2 If termination occurs after you begin the Hotel Work but before the Opening Date, you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount equal to $3,600 multiplied by the number of approved Guest Rooms at the Hotel, unless your failure to complete the Hotel Work was the result of Force Majeure.   " ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0103 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

ex:C045R0020 a ct:Rule ;
    rdfs:label "Termination — source passage 104" ;
    ct:kind "TERMINATION" ;
    ct:subject_to ex:C045R0020Condition104 ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0104 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

ex:C045R0020Condition104 a ct:Condition ;
    ct:description "14.4.1.3 If termination occurs after the Effective Date but before the second anniversary of the Opening Date, you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount equal to $3,600 multiplied by the number of approved Guest Rooms at the Hotel.   14.4.1.4 If termination occurs after the second anniversary of the Opening Date but before the final five (5) calendar years of the Term, you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount calculated by dividing the sum of the Monthly Royalty Fees due to us under this Agreement for the prior twenty-four (24) month period by twenty-four (24) and then multiplying the resulting sum by sixty (60).   14.4.1.5 If there are less than sixty (60) months remaining in the Term on the date of termination, you will pay us Liquidated Damages in an amount calculated by dividing the sum of the Monthly Royalty Fees due to us under this Agreement for the prior twenty-four (24) month period by twenty-four (24) and then multiplying the resulting sum by the number of months remaining in the Term.   14.4.2 Payment of Liquidated Damages. Payment of Liquidated Damages is due thirty (30) days following termination of this Agreement or on demand.   14.5 Actual Damages Under Special Circumstances. " ;
    ct:supported_by ex:C045P0104 ;
    meta:review_status "UNREVIEWED" .

